# ============================================================================
# Poké Emblem — Firebase Web SDK Configuration (Google Auth + Cloud Firestore)
# ============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development.
# Note: Firebase Web SDK config identifiers are public client identifiers;
# user save data is protected by `firestore.rules` (`request.auth.uid == uid`)
# and Firebase Authentication Authorized Domains.
#
# Quick Setup Steps (Firebase Console):
# 1. Go to https://console.firebase.google.com/ and create a project (e.g. `poke-emblem`).
# 2. Register a Web App (`</>`) and paste its `firebaseConfig` values below.
# 3. Enable Authentication -> Sign-in method -> Google.
#    Under Authentication -> Settings -> Authorized domains, ensure both
#    `localhost` and `adam.kenawell.family` are listed.
# 4. Create a Firestore Database (Production mode) and publish the rules from
#    `firestore.rules` at the root of this repository.
# 5. For GitHub Pages deployment, add these `PUBLIC_FIREBASE_*` keys as
#    Repository Variables (or Secrets mapped to `env:` in `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`).
# ============================================================================

PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
